   "changed": true,
   "text_before_clean": "Harriet Beecher Stowe's Personal Knowledge of the Negro Character\nBy CHARLES EDWARD STOWE\n\nIf \"Uncle Tom's Cabin\" was not true in minute particulars to plantation life, it was true to human nature in its great basilar fact that its organic elements are the same under a white or a black skin. as if it had been a plantation with seven hundred hands on it. She had lived through the whole sad history of a Virginia-raised slave's life. In her youth she must have been a very handsome",
   "role": "text"
  },
